...
Cannot read property 'user' of undefined
```
no queries or anything changed from when using `HttpLink` (which works fine)

**Edit**
When looking at the response in chrome network tab, it looks fine I can see the responses from two queries, so it seems like something goes wrong when writing to the store/cache

@peterpme: If you pause on CAUGHT exceptions you will have random errors. Apollo throws errors internally but catches / handles them

@roupen: I'm doing some research on this but I don't believe this issue is fixed yet. I think the issue below my original post got confused for the main issue. But what I'm experiencing is that BatchHttpLinks do not have response headers in the context when you attach an afterware to the link chain. I will try to research more why this is, but I believe it is because there is nothing setting the context from the response like it does in a normal HttpLink:

https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-link/blob/master/packages/apollo-link-http/src/httpLink.ts#L115

Unless I should be setting up afterware differently than I showed in the original post? Or maybe the response headers lie somewhere else but I can't find it.

Batching and credentials with apollo-link-batch-http

What about intuitive API for BatchHttpLink like the one in [example](https://www.apollographql.com/docs/react/basics/network-layer.html#) of HttpLink?

Seems to me it should look similar with BatchHttpLink to prevent dumb errors:
```js
import ApolloClient from 'apollo-client';
import { BatchHttpLink } from 'apollo-link-batch-http';

const batchLink = new BatchHttpLink({
  uri: 'https://example.com/graphql',
  // Additional fetch options like `credentials` or `headers`
  credentials: 'same-origin',
});

const client = new ApolloClient({
  batchLink,
  // other options like cache
});
```

— discussion —
@seangransee: Came here looking for this. Looks like it's already planned. From the [Batch Http Link docs](https://www.apollographql.com/docs/link/links/batch-http.html):

> Note: This package will be updated to remove the dependency on apollo-fetch an use the same options / API as the http-link

@evans: Thank you for opening an issue! We are planning to move batching into `apollo-link-http`. If you have any comments, please add them to #364!

That means that batching will use the same credentials settings as a single request.

